Here is how you can filter an array of numbers to return only the even ones using JavaScript:

```javascript
const numbers = [1, 4, 6, 7, 8, 3, 10];

// Method 1: Using the filter method
const evenNumbers = numbers.filter(num => num % 2 === 0);

console.log(evenNumbers); // Output: [4, 6, 8, 10]
```

Alternatively, you can use the `reduce` method if you prefer:

```javascript
const evenNumbers = numbers.reduce((acc, num) => {
  if (num % 2 === 0) {
    acc.push(num);
  }
  return acc;
}, []);

console.log(evenNumbers); // Output: [4, 6, 8, 10]
```

Both methods will give you the same result: `[4, 6, 8, 10]`.

